= No-contour boundary limits and final scope

The double-box no-contour work ended before either the scalar or physical
integral was generated; both were removed from the requested support and
benchmark scope. The available contour comparisons remain separate. The
massive-kite work reached a selected-boundary milestone, but no complete
interval density or full-integral benchmark.

== Algebraic boundaries and admitted local charts

The verified double-box decomposition contains *644,699 original generic-open
cells*. Its internal monotone base has 464,265 cells; that is not a smaller
complete atlas. After the positive projective anchor $x_0$, the retained lifting
order and exact catalogue complexity are:

