Degrees refer to the boundary polynomial in its current lifting variable,
not a specialized minimal polynomial. Later roots move with earlier
coordinates. Their gaps, vanishing leading coefficients, collisions, infinity
boundaries and intersections of closed faces require more than a constant-root
solver or a sampled sign check.

Native general improvements addressed parts of this problem: source-owned
constant endpoints through degree 32; exact coefficient extraction for tight
dyadic root brackets; complete recursive fan replacements; original-certificate
replay under checked positive rational scaling; and canonicalization of the
full composed measure while retaining source denominators and ancestry. They
preserve selected branches, causal phases and the Jacobian exactly once.
These operations reuse Symbolica algebra and symGCAD certificates; they do not
constitute an automatic resolver for every moving boundary.#footnote[
